GTK Interface is a separate program.  You DL it, install it, then run it 
via a shortcut icon (or just double click gthack,exe).  It should be 
installed in a different location that where you have SlashEm installed (at 
least mine is and it works great).  When you run it, it will prompt you for 
a SlashEm server to connect to.  Select wherever you have SlashEm 
installed, then select slashem.exe and press Connect.  It will load that 
location, run the SlashEm executable and you will be off and running.

